# Standard Coding Practices

Calculations, derivations, formatting, filtering, mapping, and predicates belong in pure helper functions. Components, hooks, route handlers, and other callers invoke those helpers. They do not inline the logic.

A helper is pure when the same arguments always produce the same result, it does not read or write React state, and it does not perform I/O. Pass time, randomness, and loaded records in as arguments. Do not mutate arguments; return a new value.

Name the helper for the result the caller gets (`episodesRemaining`, `formatActivityClock`), and keep it next to the feature that owns the rule (usually a `services/` module). Document it the way that module requires.

## Encapsulate logic in pure helpers

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — progress math and copy are trapped in the component
export function ContinueWatchingRow({ item }: { item: ContinueWatchingItem }) {
  const remaining = Math.max(item.episodeCount - item.episodesWatched, 0)
  const label = remaining === 1 ? '1 episode left' : `${remaining} episodes left`

  return <CardDescription>{label}</CardDescription>
}

// ✅ GOOD — the rule lives in a pure helper; the component only calls it
/** Episodes still unwatched. Never negative. */
export function episodesRemaining(episodeCount: number, episodesWatched: number): number {
  return Math.max(episodeCount - episodesWatched, 0)
}

/** Short continue-watching label for a remaining-episode count. */
export function episodesRemainingLabel(remaining: number): string {
  return remaining === 1 ? '1 episode left' : `${remaining} episodes left`
}

export function ContinueWatchingRow({ item }: { item: ContinueWatchingItem }) {
  const label = episodesRemainingLabel(episodesRemaining(item.episodeCount, item.episodesWatched))

  return <CardDescription>{label}</CardDescription>
}
```

## Existing code

Refactor opportunistically. When a change touches code that breaks these rules, bring that code into compliance as part of the change. Do not leave a violation in code you are already editing. Limit the refactor to the module you are changing and the helpers it needs. Do not start a repository-wide rewrite only to apply this ruleset.
